>
  <p>Parging is the thin cement-based coat on the exposed band of your foundation, and it does two jobs at once: it shields the wall from moisture and weather, and it gives the base of the building a clean, finished look. <a href="/">Concrete Toronto</a> parges walls, basements and more across Toronto and the GTA, keeping your buildings protected and presentable.</p>

  <p>When a parge coat starts to crack, flake or bubble, the wall underneath takes the weather directly. Water works in behind the loose coat, frost pries it further, and by spring the patches have become sheets. Catching it early is a small, quick job. Waiting means more prep and a bigger repair.</p>

  <h2>What's included in our parging service</h2>
  <p>Every parging job is priced as a complete package in a written quote:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Foundation wall parging</strong> on the exposed band above grade</li>
    <li><strong>Basement parging</strong> for interior walls that need a clean, sealed finish</li>
    <li><strong>Parging repair</strong> for cracks, flaking and sections that have let go</li>
    <li><strong>Proper prep</strong>: loose material removed, surface cleaned, coat bonded so it stays put</li>
    <li><strong>Waterproofing</strong> to protect concrete foundations from water damage</li>
    <li><strong>Full cleanup</strong> when the work is done</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Parging and waterproofing together</h2>
  <p>Parging sheds surface water, but it is not a substitute for waterproofing where water is actively getting in. We provide waterproofing services to protect concrete foundations from water damage, and we will tell you plainly which one your wall needs. Often the right answer is both: waterproof where the water pressure is, parge where the wall shows.</p>

  <h2>Why homeowners choose us</h2>
  <p>Concrete and parging are the same trade to us: cement, prep and patience. 15 years of local work, a 2-year warranty, and a satisfaction guarantee on every job.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>2-year warranty on our work</li>
    <li>Satisfaction guaranteed</li>
    <li>Free, no-obligation quotes</li>
  </ul>

